{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 180 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "82ce805daae17ad2b248a9f9bce5c0353b61be6d364879d725d2b5cbd5449746" :edb/db-before-t 179 :edb/db-after-t 180 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533492 50 #inst "2026-10-11T02:48:08.000Z" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186059854 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403341 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186060401 1068 #edb/ref 17592186058998 13194139533492 17592186045585 false] [17592186060401 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403495 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186060401 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186060401 1071 "What would be the system of equations for the following augmented matrix?\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 10 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186060401 1071 "What would be the system of equations for the following augmented matrix?\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 10 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139533492 17592186045585 false] [17592186060401 1074 "The augmented matrix consists of two parts: the coefficient matrix and the column of constants.\n\nThe coefficient matrix represents the coefficients in the linear system, while the column of constants represents the constants on the right-hand sides of the equations.\n\nUsing the variables $x$ and  $y$,  the corresponding system of equations is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-2y=10 \\\\ -x+y=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186068906 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403467 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186078489 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403543 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186079202 1068 #edb/ref 17592186077960 13194139533492 17592186045585 false] [17592186079202 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403550 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186079202 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186079202 1071 "The acceleration $a$ at time $t$ of a particle $P$ moving in the $xy$-plane is given by\n\n$$\na(t)=⟨6t-2,4⟩.\n$$\n\nGiven that the particle is at the position $(0,0)$ and has velocity $⟨1,\\,4⟩$ when $t=1,$ calculate the position vector of $P$ at time $t.$" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186079202 1071 "The acceleration $a$ at time $t$ of a particle $P$ moving in the $xy$-plane is given by\n$a(t) = ⟨6t - 2, 4⟩$.\nGiven that the particle is at the position $(0, 0)$ and has velocity $⟨1, 4⟩$ when $t = 1$, calculate the position vector of $P$ at time $t$." 13194139533492 17592186045585 false] [17592186079202 1074 "To compute the position vector, we need to integrate the velocity vector. To find the velocity vector, we first need to integrate the acceleration vector. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int ⟨6t-2,4⟩\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨\\int (6t-2)\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int 4\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{t}^{2}-2t+{C}_{1},\\,4t+{C}_{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve for the constants of integration using the fact that $v(1)=⟨1,4⟩.$ Substituting $t=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(1) & =⟨3(1)^{2}-2(1)+{C}_{1},\\,4(1)+{C}_{2}⟩ \\\\ ⟨1,4⟩ & =⟨1+{C}_{1},4+{C}_{2}⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso we must have ${C}_{1}=0$ and ${C}_{2}=0.$ Therefore, the velocity vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =⟨3{t}^{2}-2t,\\,4t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the position vector by integrating the velocity vector.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =\\int v(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int ⟨3{t}^{2}-2t,\\,4t⟩\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨\\int (3{t}^{2}-2t)\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int 4t\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{3}-{t}^{2}+{C}_{3},\\,2{t}^{2}+{C}_{4}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve for the constants of integration using the fact that $r(1)=⟨0,0⟩.$ Substituting $t=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(1) & =⟨(1)^{3}-(1)^{2}+{C}_{3},\\,2(1)^{2}+{C}_{4}⟩ \\\\ ⟨0,0⟩ & =⟨{C}_{3},2+{C}_{4}⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso we must have ${C}_{3}=0$ and ${C}_{4}=-2.$ Therefore, the position of $P$ at time $t$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨{t}^{3}-{t}^{2},\\,2{t}^{2}-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186083246 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403285 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186087701 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403292 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186087701 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403299 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186087703 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403306 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186087708 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403515 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186087708 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403522 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186087719 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403334 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186087730 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403348 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186087735 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403355 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186087739 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403411 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186087748 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403313 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186087748 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403327 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186087828 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403556 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186096622 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403418 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186110581 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403383 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186110593 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403390 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186110594 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403397 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186110594 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403404 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186110724 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403362 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186115239 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403501 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186124451 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403481 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186124470 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403474 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186124512 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403376 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186124513 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403425 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186124513 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403529 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186129167 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403488 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186152193 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403320 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186175932 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403536 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186176105 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403508 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186184339 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403369 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186198355 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403432 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186198355 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403446 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186198439 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403439 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186198439 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403453 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186198439 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403460 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403285 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403286 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403285 1069 "q-6836" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403285 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403285 1071 "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=12\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=15\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,\n$$\n\n calculate $\\frac{dy}{dx}.$" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403285 1072 #uuid "b50faac3-57b3-5534-a1d3-8f76087cb51c" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403285 1074 "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(\\theta )}{{x}^{′}(\\theta )}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(\\theta )=12\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,{y}^{′}(\\theta )=-15\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{-15\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{12\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }=-\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta .\n$$" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403286 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403287 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403286 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403288 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403286 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403289 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403286 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403290 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403286 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403291 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403286 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403286 1077 "selection" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403286 1079 #edb/ref 17592186403290 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403286 1080 #uuid "81664d19-fcb9-599f-8db6-ec3e35d93bb8" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403287 1081 "\\frac{dy}{dx}=-\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta " 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403287 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403287 1084 #uuid "1dc882f2-3f87-5d1b-873e-989959c29c45" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403288 1081 "\\frac{dy}{dx}=-\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta " 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403288 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403288 1084 #uuid "571f5f41-efb0-58e5-a46f-8c213ca0a973" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403289 1081 "\\frac{dy}{dx}=-\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta " 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403289 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403289 1084 #uuid "73cec9e6-12bd-5c23-9094-78dadbc4e7d9" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403290 1081 "\\frac{dy}{dx}=-\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta " 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403290 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403290 1084 #uuid "a99bf228-d02b-5fa9-b6b7-158b7cd89312" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403291 1081 "\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta " 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403291 10