98 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403498 1084 #uuid "f08977b3-da5b-5a3f-9b5f-51a1b0b73af2" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403499 1081 "{\\begin{aligned}x+2y=10 \\\\ x+y=-2\\end{aligned}" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403499 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403499 1084 #uuid "d79b540e-61c1-524a-aada-7bc8f0c88fc5" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403500 1081 "{\\begin{aligned}x+2y=1 \\\\ -x+y=-2\\end{aligned}" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403500 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403500 1084 #uuid "a1094fb0-5cb4-5005-a45b-91f8fd20411a" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403501 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403502 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403501 1069 "q-71854" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403501 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403501 1071 "What is the system of equations represented by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 12\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -15\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403501 1072 #uuid "7f74fa12-0053-502d-b17f-669ab25e05d2" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403501 1074 "The  $2\\times 2$ matrix represents the coefficients of $x$ and $y,$ while the $2\\times 1$ column vector on the right-hand side represents the constants of the equations. So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}0x-y=0 \\\\ -3x+12y=-15.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying both equations in the system, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}y=0 \\\\ x-4y=5.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403502 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403503 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403502 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403504 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403502 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403505 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403502 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403506 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403502 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403507 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403502 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403502 1077 "selection" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403502 1079 #edb/ref 17592186403503 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403502 1080 #uuid "796fd7cb-3aaa-51b5-a9d2-6f0f250be044" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403503 1081 "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}y=0 \\\\ x-4y=5\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403503 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403503 1084 #uuid "f2b0257b-5aa5-5961-8c79-b270612973ca" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403504 1081 "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}y=0 \\\\ -4x+y=5\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403504 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403504 1084 #uuid "efe4f88d-8258-5d39-be46-855c1e2c58e1" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403505 1081 "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x=0 \\\\ x-4y=5\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403505 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403505 1084 #uuid "7cea8dbe-3578-5886-bfe4-f51b25347ed9" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403506 1081 "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}y=5 \\\\ x-4y=0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403506 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403506 1084 #uuid "aba3c242-ef16-5d89-8d0a-32ce47931725" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403507 1081 "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x=0 \\\\ x-3y=5\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403507 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403507 1084 #uuid "777783df-e9bd-5dfd-9c9a-d3ccfc310aa7" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403508 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403509 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403508 1069 "q-7188" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403508 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403508 1071 "A particle $P$ is traveling along the $x$-axis with displacement $s(t)$ from a fixed origin $O$ given by\n\n$$\ns(t)=-\\frac{2}{9}{t}^{3}+3{t}^{2}+14t+17,\\,t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nFind the time at which the acceleration is zero, and find the value of the velocity at this moment." 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403508 1072 #uuid "e823f661-78ed-5c49-931f-9f7b092bd2fe" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403508 1074 "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\frac{2}{9}{t}^{3}+3{t}^{2}+14t+17) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}{t}^{2}+6t+14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\frac{2}{3}{t}^{2}+6t+14) \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}t+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we put $a=0$ to find the time when the acceleration is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & =-\\frac{4}{3}t+6 \\\\ \\frac{4}{3}t & =6 \\\\ t & =4.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the acceleration is zero when $t=4.5.$ To find the velocity at this moment, we substitute this back into $v(t)$ to get\n\n$$\nv(4.5)=-\\frac{2}{3}(4.5)^{2}+6(4.5)+14=27.5.\n$$" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403509 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403510 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403509 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403511 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403509 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403512 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403509 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403513 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403509 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403514 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403509 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403509 1077 "selection" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403509 1079 #edb/ref 17592186403511 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403509 1080 #uuid "f245a54a-e7b7-5958-90da-5850b106775b" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403510 1081 "t=4,\\,v=10.75" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403510 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403510 1084 #uuid "e800b9e5-7a04-5a52-83f0-e3afcf5ec850" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403511 1081 "t=4.5,\\,v=27.5" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403511 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403511 1084 #uuid "353897c1-d771-528a-9201-b28cc593f791" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403512 1081 "t=4.5,\\,v=12" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403512 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403512 1084 #uuid "351b1c52-f2f1-52fc-bd66-0b6482b93763" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403513 1081 "t=3.5,\\,v=26.5" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403513 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403513 1084 #uuid "e50e1c45-ecbd-5feb-9363-3cbef9942625" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403514 1081 "t=4,\\,v=22.5" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403514 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403514 1084 #uuid "61d395f2-5e29-597d-bed3-c8a2e676c54f" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403515 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403516 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403515 1069 "q-71935" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403515 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403515 1071 "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\n$$\nN=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,Z=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403515 1072 #uuid "5f5bb9d1-db59-54f4-aa53-0a0fa0a6f6c0" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403515 1074 "- For the matrix $N$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(N)=3\\cdot 0-0\\cdot 1=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(N)=0,$ we conclude that $N$ is not invertible. Since $N$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $N$ is singular.\n\n- The matrix $V$ is a $5\\times 1$ matrix. So, it is not invertible. Since the matrix is not square, we can't say that it's singular.\n\n- For the matrix $Z$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(Z)=0\\cdot 0-2\\cdot 8=-16.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(Z)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $Z$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $N$ is singular." 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403516 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403517 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403516 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403518 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403516 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403519 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403516 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403520 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403516 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403521 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403516 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403516 1077 "selection" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403516 1079 #edb/ref 17592186403519 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403516 1080 #uuid "4c8f2087-255d-5d6d-a82b-15aea897bf14" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403517 1081 "$Z$ only" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403517 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403517 1084 #uuid "5ba36d58-d1d6-5ff0-b69b-11b2c1c1f333" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403518 1081 "$V$ and $Z$ only" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403518 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403518 1084 #uuid "a03c5260-c217-57dd-b98f-2ac534243676" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403519 1081 "$N$ only" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403519 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403519 1084 #uuid "443e1475-f514-591e-a0cb-e3f1e1654880" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403520 1081 "$N$ and $V$ only" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403520 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403520 1084 #uuid "5eb55277-5738-59bc-a22d-d8bc11aa5ca7" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403521 1081 "$N$ and $Z$ only" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403521 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403521 1084 #uuid "f0611bed-cd36-5759-ab42-7367446353e4" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403522 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403523 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403522 1069 "q-71937" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403522 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403522 1071 "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -8 & 7 & -6 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3 & -4\\end{aligned}],\\,U=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -15 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 10 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403522 1072 #uuid "ff070848-777f-5635-9918-6da54f4ec8b2" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403522 1074 "- The matrix $T$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix. So, it is not invertible. Since the matrix is not square, we can't say that it's singular.\n\n- For the matrix $U$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(U)=3\\cdot 4-(-1)\\cdot (-15)=-3.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(U)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $U$ is invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $V$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(V)=6\\cdot 5-10\\cdot 3=0.\n$$\n\nBecause 