,\\,t=2\\,\\text{s}" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403542 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403542 1084 #uuid "76ad20db-ee5e-5f32-b5be-14cbb55e6f65" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403543 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403544 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403543 1069 "q-7217" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403543 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403543 1071 "The velocity $v$ at time $t$ of a particle $P$ moving in the $xy$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nv=⟨t(3t-2),\\,8{t}^{3}⟩.\n$$\n\nGiven that the particle is at the position $(30,90)$ when $t=3,$ calculate the position vector of $P$ at time $t.$" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403543 1072 #uuid "4e1070d0-6a3b-5c88-bdfe-23bfbc7b2d02" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403543 1074 "To compute the position vector, we need to integrate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =\\int v(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int ⟨t(3t-2),\\,8{t}^{3}⟩\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨\\int t(3t-2)\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int 8{t}^{3}\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{3}-{t}^{2}+{C}_{1},\\,2{t}^{4}+{C}_{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve for the constants of integration using the fact that $r(3)=⟨30,90⟩.$ Substituting $t=3,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(3) & =⟨(3)^{3}-(3)^{2}+{C}_{1},\\,2(3)^{4}+{C}_{2}⟩ \\\\ ⟨30,90⟩ & =⟨18+{C}_{1},162+{C}_{2}⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso we must have ${C}_{1}=12$ and ${C}_{2}=-72.$ Therefore, the position vector is\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨{t}^{3}-{t}^{2}+12,\\,2{t}^{4}-72⟩.\n$$" 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403544 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403545 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403544 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403546 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403544 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403547 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403544 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403548 13194139533492 17592186045585 true] [17592186403544 1075 #edb/ref 1759218